            <ArticleTitle>Hybrid approach combining off-pump CABG with transapical aortic valve implantation via median sternotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0031-1280018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 75-year-old patient diagnosed with severe aortic stenosis and two-vessel coronary artery disease. Due to multiple comorbidities including chronic renal insufficiency, stroke and pulmonary hypertension (EuroSCORE: 34%; STS mortality risk: 14.9%), he was not a candidate for conventional aortic valve surgery. He underwent a novel hybrid treatment approach combining off-pump CABG and transapical aortic valve implantation via a median sternotomy. Extracorporeal circulation could be entirely avoided.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Thieme Medical Publishers 333 Seventh Avenue, New York, NY 10001, USA.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
